{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:19:12.016Z","ordinal":68171,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","session_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","root_turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","response_id":"resp_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac61c99951887d0ae03761384c85f99","usage":{"input_tokens":71387,"cached_input_tokens":61568,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":169,"reasoning_output_tokens":59,"total_tokens":71556},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":37960604,"cached_input_tokens":37202816,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":186890,"reasoning_output_tokens":74592,"total_tokens":38147494},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1274470806,"cached_input_tokens":1248226304,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6324952,"reasoning_output_tokens":2824429,"total_tokens":1280795758}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:19:12.089Z","ordinal":68172,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-082d62c2-fe42-43a5-8ceb-0a46df953877","process_id":"22197","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '538,570p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md\nsed -n '725,750p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json\ncat packages/api/rpc/src/live.layer.ts\ncat packages/analytics/src/errors.ts packages/analytics/src/service.ts\ncat packages/analytics/tsconfig.json packages/analytics/vitest.config.ts"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '538,570p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md\nsed -n '725,750p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json\ncat packages/api/rpc/src/live.layer.ts\ncat packages/analytics/src/errors.ts packages/analytics/src/service.ts\ncat packages/analytics/tsconfig.json packages/analytics/vitest.config.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Manage retained TaxKit Production and one shared Preview PostHog project through\nAlchemy, following Common Practice's fixed US-region pattern, subject to the\nactual organisation/credentials in the reviewed provider plan. Local analytics\nis disabled. Ordinary Previews are disabled; an explicit controlled Preview\nproof can enable its Preview project. Production capture tokens are public\nwrite-only browser inputs; management/query credentials remain private in\nDoppler and never enter app output or bundles. No paid feature or billing\nchange is required by this scope.\n\nUse a private Effect browser service and React-owned Atom lifetime around the\nlatest `posthog-js`. Explicitly disable autocapture, recording, person profiles,\nsurveys and unnecessary automatic events; set Do Not Track handling explicitly.\nUse memory persistence with persistence disabled, rather than assuming local\nstorage cannot fall back to cookies. Qualify current shutdown/flush behaviour\nwithout promising network delivery on tab close. A synchronous closed allowlist\nafter SDK enrichment rejects unknown events/fields. Anonymous event identity\nand checked page metadata are the only browser context needed.\nKeep explicitly configured-off analytics distinct from invalid configuration:\ninvalid project/region/stage/token configuration has a named checked failure,\nnot a silent disabled result. After valid initialisation, capture/delivery is\nbest-effort and cannot fail a tax calculation or page. There is no old consent\nor identity migration to copy into the fresh application.\n\nThe Website may own a narrow same-origin POST event relay as the skill's\nanalytics exception to separate machine routes. Fix its regional upstream,\nchecked origin, path, query and media types. Bound whole-body read, forwarded\nbytes, upstream wait and reply size. Strip cookies, authorisation, IP-forwarding\nand tracing headers; do not follow or expose redirects. Preserve event UUIDs,\ntimestamps and upstream status; keep no-store. The SDK owns retries and the relay\nmakes one upstream attempt. Qualify the current SDK's actual `/e/` endpoint,\nbatch/compression/query behaviour; do not copy an older relay contract blindly.\n\n## Shared Axiom telemetry\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-008\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T004\",\n        \"CSF-T005\",\n        \"CSF-T006\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Manage retained TaxKit Production and shared Preview projects through a private Alchemy Resource/Provider and current Distilled PostHog, with checked organisation/region/ownership and safe management failures.\",\n        \"Implement explicit pageviews in a private React-owned browser service and one successful hosted-calculation event owner in the backend application; honour a checked browser opt-out without linking identities.\",\n        \"Use a synchronous final-enrichment allowlist, memory-only persistence, explicit DNT and disabled automatic/replay/person features. Local and ordinary Preview capture stay off; no consent dialog.\",\n        \"Implement the bounded same-origin event relay and native backend capture through owned Effect HTTP. Qualify actual current SDK transport/disposal and no duplicate events; retain best-effort delivery limits.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"apps/web analytics service/live adapter/consumer/relay and route event ownership\",\n        \"apps/api application successful-use capture and checked collection policy\",\n        \"packages/infrastructure PostHog provider/resources/bindings and qualified optional provider fixes\",\n        \"Analytics tests, app/infra READMEs, privacy/public copy and deployment/recovery runbook sections\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run test\",\n        \"bun run test:oxlint\",\nimport type {\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\n  DescriptorFilterQuery,\n  GetCalculatorGraphRequest,\n  GetCalculatorRequest,\n  MetadataQuery,\n} from \"@taxkit/calculators/schemas\";\nimport { Array, Effect, Layer, Schema } from \"effect\";\nimport type { Scope } from \"effect\";\nimport { FetchHttpClient, HttpClient, HttpClientRequest } from \"effect/http\";\nimport type { RpcClientError } from \"effect/rpc\";\nimport { Rpc, RpcClient, RpcSerialization } from \"effect/rpc\";\n\nimport {\n  boundedCalculatorRpcHttpClient,\n  calculatorRpcTransportFailure,\n} from \"./client-response.boundary.js\";\nimport type { CalculatorRpcExpectedError } from \"./errors.js\";\nimport {\n  CalculatorRpcDeadlineExceeded,\n  CalculatorRpcInvalidResponse,\n} from \"./errors.js\";\nimport { TaxKitRpcGroup } from \"./group.js\";\nimport { CalculatorRpcDeadline, CalculatorRpcVersion } from \"./schemas.js\";\nimport type { CalculatorRpcOrigin } from \"./schemas.js\";\nimport { TaxKitRpcClient } from \"./service.js\";\n\nclass RpcReplyDecodeDefect extends Schema.TaggedError<RpcReplyDecodeDefect>()(\n  \"RpcReplyDecodeDefect\",\n  {}\n) {}\n\n// Effect 4 caches the native exit Schema. Mark only its reply decoder's failure;\n// an independent adapter SchemaError remains a defect with its original identity.\nconst replySerialization = Layer.succeed(\n  RpcSerialization.RpcSerialization,\n  RpcSerialization.RpcSerialization.of({\n    ...RpcSerialization.json,\n    codecFor: <S extends Schema.Top>(schema: S) => {\n      const codec = RpcSerialization.json.codecFor(schema);\n      return Array.some(\n        Array.fromIterable(TaxKitRpcGroup.requests.values()),\n        (procedure) => schema.ast === Rpc.exitSchema(procedure).ast\n      )\n        ? codec.pipe(\n            Schema.catchDecoding<typeof codec>(() =>\n              Effect.die(new RpcReplyDecodeDefect())\n            )\n          )\n        : codec;\n    },\n  })\n);\n\n// The concrete native operation owns its client scope, complete-response budget\n// and safe failure projection. This accepts an Effect, never a raw-client callback.\nconst checkedRpcOperation = <A>(\n  operation: Effect.Effect<\n    A,\n    typeof CalculatorRpcExpectedError.Type | RpcClientError.RpcClientError,\n    Scope.Scope | RpcClient.Protocol\n  >,\n  protocol: RpcClient.Protocol[\"Service\"]\n) =>\n  operation.pipe(\n    Effect.scoped,\n    Effect.provideService(RpcClient.Protocol, protocol),\n    Effect.provideService(HttpClient.TracerDisabledWhen, () => true),\n    Effect.provideService(FetchHttpClient.RequestInit, {\n      credentials: \"omit\",\n      redirect: \"error\",\n    }),\n    Effect.timeoutOrElse({\n      duration: CalculatorRpcDeadline,\n      orElse: () => Effect.fail(new CalculatorRpcDeadlineExceeded()),\n    }),\n    Effect.catchTag(\"RpcClientError\", (error) =>\n      Effect.fail(calculatorRpcTransportFailure(error))\n    ),\n    Effect.catchDefect((defect) =>\n      Schema.is(RpcReplyDecodeDefect)(defect)\n        ? Effect.fail(new CalculatorRpcInvalidResponse())\n        : Effect.die(defect)\n    )\n  );\n\n// The app supplies its matching-stage HttpClient. The Layer retains transport\n// configuration, while each named operation owns its native client scope. A\n// Worker can suspend between requests: retaining a receive-loop fibre acquired\n// by an earlier request leaves later calls waiting. No runtime or Layer is built\n// by a calculation; native RPC creation and finalisation run in its own scope.\nexport const TaxKitRpcClientLive = (origin: CalculatorRpcOrigin) =>\n  Layer.effect(\n    TaxKitRpcClient,\n    Effect.gen(function* () {\n      const protocol = yield* RpcClient.Protocol;\n      return TaxKitRpcClient.of({\n        calculate: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.calculate\")(\n          (request: CalculatorRunServiceRequest) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.Calculate({ request, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        getCalculator: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.getCalculator\")(\n          (request: GetCalculatorRequest) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.GetCalculator({\n                    request,\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\n                  })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        getCalculatorGraph: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.getCalculatorGraph\")(\n          (request: GetCalculatorGraphRequest) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.GetCalculatorGraph({\n                    request,\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\n                  })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        getCalculatorSchema: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.getCalculatorSchema\")(\n          (request: GetCalculatorRequest) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.GetCalculatorSchema({\n                    request,\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\n                  })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        listCalculators: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listCalculators\")(\n          (query: MetadataQuery) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.ListCalculators({\n                    query,\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\n                  })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        listFacts: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listFacts\")(\n          (query: DescriptorFilterQuery) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.ListFacts({ query, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        listJurisdictions: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listJurisdictions\")(() =>\n          checkedRpcOperation(\n            RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n              Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                client.ListJurisdictions({ version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n              )\n            ),\n            protocol\n          )\n        ),\n        listRules: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listRules\")(\n          (query: DescriptorFilterQuery) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.ListRules({ query, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        listTaxYears: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listTaxYears\")(\n          (query: MetadataQuery) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.ListTaxYears({ query, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n      });\n    })\n  ).pipe(\n    Layer.provide(\n      Layer.effect(\n        RpcClient.Protocol,\n        HttpClient.HttpClient.pipe(\n          Effect.map((client) =>\n            client.pipe(\n              HttpClient.mapRequest(\n                HttpClientRequest.setUrl(new URL(\"/rpc\", origin).href)\n              ),\n              boundedCalculatorRpcHttpClient\n            )\n          ),\n          Effect.flatMap(RpcClient.makeProtocolHttp)\n        )\n      )\n    ),\n    Layer.provide(replySerialization)\n  );\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\";\n\nexport class AnalyticsConfigurationError extends Schema.TaggedError<AnalyticsConfigurationError>()(\n  \"AnalyticsConfigurationError\", { operation: Schema.Literal(\"configure\") }\n) {}\nexport class AnalyticsCaptureError extends Schema.TaggedError<AnalyticsCaptureError>()(\n  \"AnalyticsCaptureError\", {\n    operation: Schema.Literals([\"pageview\", \"calculator-use\", \"shutdown\"]),\n    reason: Schema.Literals([\"transport\", \"rejected\", \"deadline\", \"encoding\", \"identity\", \"response-size\", \"sdk\", \"closed\"]),\n  }\n) {}\nimport { Context } from \"effect\";\nimport type { Effect } from \"effect\";\nimport type { AnalyticsCaptureError } from \"./errors.js\";\nimport type { CalculatorUse, CaptureDisposition, CollectionPolicy, PageView } from \"./schemas.js\";\n\nexport class BackendAnalytics extends Context.Service<BackendAnalytics, {\n  readonly recordCalculatorUse: (input: CalculatorUse) => Effect.Effect<CaptureDisposition, AnalyticsCaptureError>;\n}>()(\"@taxkit/analytics/BackendAnalytics\") {}\nexport class BrowserAnalytics extends Context.Service<BrowserAnalytics, {\n  readonly recordPageView: (input: PageView) => Effect.Effect<CaptureDisposition, AnalyticsCaptureError>;\n  readonly getCollectionPolicy: Effect.Effect<CollectionPolicy, AnalyticsCaptureError>;\n}>()(\"@taxkit/analytics/BrowserAnalytics\") {}\n{\n  \"extends\": \"../../tsconfig.base.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2024\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"include\": [\n    \"src/**/*.ts\",\n    \"test/**/*.ts\",\n    \"vitest.config.ts\"\n  ]\n}\nimport { defaultServerConditions } from \"vite\";\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  resolve: { conditions: [\"source\", ...defaultServerConditions] },\n  test: { fileParallelism: false, include: [\"test/**/*.test.ts\"] },\n});\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Manage retained TaxKit Production and one shared Preview PostHog project through\nAlchemy, following Common Practice's fixed US-region pattern, subject to the\nactual organisation/credentials in the reviewed provider plan. Local analytics\nis disabled. Ordinary Previews are disabled; an explicit controlled Preview\nproof can enable its Preview project. Production capture tokens are public\nwrite-only browser inputs; management/query credentials remain private in\nDoppler and never enter app output or bundles. No paid feature or billing\nchange is required by this scope.\n\nUse a private Effect browser service and React-owned Atom lifetime around the\nlatest `posthog-js`. Explicitly disable autocapture, recording, person profiles,\nsurveys and unnecessary automatic events; set Do Not Track handling explicitly.\nUse memory persistence with persistence disabled, rather than assuming local\nstorage cannot fall back to cookies. Qualify current shutdown/flush behaviour\nwithout promising network delivery on tab close. A synchronous closed allowlist\nafter SDK enrichment rejects unknown events/fields. Anonymous event identity\nand checked page metadata are the only browser context needed.\nKeep explicitly configured-off analytics distinct from invalid configuration:\ninvalid project/region/stage/token configuration has a named checked failure,\nnot a silent disabled result. After valid initialisation, capture/delivery is\nbest-effort and cannot fail a tax calculation or page. There is no old consent\nor identity migration to copy into the fresh application.\n\nThe Website may own a narrow same-origin POST event relay as the skill's\nanalytics exception to separate machine routes. Fix its regional upstream,\nchecked origin, path, query and media types. Bound whole-body read, forwarded\nbytes, upstream wait and reply size. Strip cookies, authorisation, IP-forwarding\nand tracing headers; do not follow or expose redirects. Preserve event UUIDs,\ntimestamps and upstream status; keep no-store. The SDK owns retries and the relay\nmakes one upstream attempt. Qualify the current SDK's actual `/e/` endpoint,\nbatch/compression/query behaviour; do not copy an older relay contract blindly.\n\n## Shared Axiom telemetry\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-008\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T004\",\n        \"CSF-T005\",\n        \"CSF-T006\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Manage retained TaxKit Production and shared Preview projects through a private Alchemy Resource/Provider and current Distilled PostHog, with checked organisation/region/ownership and safe management failures.\",\n        \"Implement explicit pageviews in a private React-owned browser service and one successful hosted-calculation event owner in the backend application; honour a checked browser opt-out without linking identities.\",\n        \"Use a synchronous final-enrichment allowlist, memory-only persistence, explicit DNT and disabled automatic/replay/person features. Local and ordinary Preview capture stay off; no consent dialog.\",\n        \"Implement the bounded same-origin event relay and native backend capture through owned Effect HTTP. Qualify actual current SDK transport/disposal and no duplicate events; retain best-effort delivery limits.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"apps/web analytics service/live adapter/consumer/relay and route event ownership\",\n        \"apps/api application successful-use capture and checked collection policy\",\n        \"packages/infrastructure PostHog provider/resources/bindings and qualified optional provider fixes\",\n        \"Analytics tests, app/infra READMEs, privacy/public copy and deployment/recovery runbook sections\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run test\",\n        \"bun run test:oxlint\",\nimport type {\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\n  DescriptorFilterQuery,\n  GetCalculatorGraphRequest,\n  GetCalculatorRequest,\n  MetadataQuery,\n} from \"@taxkit/calculators/schemas\";\nimport { Array, Effect, Layer, Schema } from \"effect\";\nimport type { Scope } from \"effect\";\nimport { FetchHttpClient, HttpClient, HttpClientRequest } from \"effect/http\";\nimport type { RpcClientError } from \"effect/rpc\";\nimport { Rpc, RpcClient, RpcSerialization } from \"effect/rpc\";\n\nimport {\n  boundedCalculatorRpcHttpClient,\n  calculatorRpcTransportFailure,\n} from \"./client-response.boundary.js\";\nimport type { CalculatorRpcExpectedError } from \"./errors.js\";\nimport {\n  CalculatorRpcDeadlineExceeded,\n  CalculatorRpcInvalidResponse,\n} from \"./errors.js\";\nimport { TaxKitRpcGroup } from \"./group.js\";\nimport { CalculatorRpcDeadline, CalculatorRpcVersion } from \"./schemas.js\";\nimport type { CalculatorRpcOrigin } from \"./schemas.js\";\nimport { TaxKitRpcClient } from \"./service.js\";\n\nclass RpcReplyDecodeDefect extends Schema.TaggedError<RpcReplyDecodeDefect>()(\n  \"RpcReplyDecodeDefect\",\n  {}\n) {}\n\n// Effect 4 caches the native exit Schema. Mark only its reply decoder's failure;\n// an independent adapter SchemaError remains a defect with its original identity.\nconst replySerialization = Layer.succeed(\n  RpcSerialization.RpcSerialization,\n  RpcSerialization.RpcSerialization.of({\n    ...RpcSerialization.json,\n    codecFor: <S extends Schema.Top>(schema: S) => {\n      const codec = RpcSerialization.json.codecFor(schema);\n      return Array.some(\n        Array.fromIterable(TaxKitRpcGroup.requests.values()),\n        (procedure) => schema.ast === Rpc.exitSchema(procedure).ast\n      )\n        ? codec.pipe(\n            Schema.catchDecoding<typeof codec>(() =>\n              Effect.die(new RpcReplyDecodeDefect())\n            )\n          )\n        : codec;\n    },\n  })\n);\n\n// The concrete native operation owns its client scope, complete-response budget\n// and safe failure projection. This accepts an Effect, never a raw-client callback.\nconst checkedRpcOperation = <A>(\n  operation: Effect.Effect<\n    A,\n    typeof CalculatorRpcExpectedError.Type | RpcClientError.RpcClientError,\n    Scope.Scope | RpcClient.Protocol\n  >,\n  protocol: RpcClient.Protocol[\"Service\"]\n) =>\n  operation.pipe(\n    Effect.scoped,\n    Effect.provideService(RpcClient.Protocol, protocol),\n    Effect.provideService(HttpClient.TracerDisabledWhen, () => true),\n    Effect.provideService(FetchHttpClient.RequestInit, {\n      credentials: \"omit\",\n      redirect: \"error\",\n    }),\n    Effect.timeoutOrElse({\n      duration: CalculatorRpcDeadline,\n      orElse: () => Effect.fail(new CalculatorRpcDeadlineExceeded()),\n    }),\n    Effect.catchTag(\"RpcClientError\", (error) =>\n      Effect.fail(calculatorRpcTransportFailure(error))\n    ),\n    Effect.catchDefect((defect) =>\n      Schema.is(RpcReplyDecodeDefect)(defect)\n        ? Effect.fail(new CalculatorRpcInvalidResponse())\n        : Effect.die(defect)\n    )\n  );\n\n// The app supplies its matching-stage HttpClient. The Layer retains transport\n// configuration, while each named operation owns its native client scope. A\n// Worker can suspend between requests: retaining a receive-loop fibre acquired\n// by an earlier request leaves later calls waiting. No runtime or Layer is built\n// by a calculation; native RPC creation and finalisation run in its own scope.\nexport const TaxKitRpcClientLive = (origin: CalculatorRpcOrigin) =>\n  Layer.effect(\n    TaxKitRpcClient,\n    Effect.gen(function* () {\n      const protocol = yield* RpcClient.Protocol;\n      return TaxKitRpcClient.of({\n        calculate: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.calculate\")(\n          (request: CalculatorRunServiceRequest) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.Calculate({ request, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        getCalculator: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.getCalculator\")(\n          (request: GetCalculatorRequest) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.GetCalculator({\n                    request,\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\n                  })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        getCalculatorGraph: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.getCalculatorGraph\")(\n          (request: GetCalculatorGraphRequest) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.GetCalculatorGraph({\n                    request,\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\n                  })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        getCalculatorSchema: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.getCalculatorSchema\")(\n          (request: GetCalculatorRequest) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.GetCalculatorSchema({\n                    request,\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\n                  })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        listCalculators: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listCalculators\")(\n          (query: MetadataQuery) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.ListCalculators({\n                    query,\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\n                  })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        listFacts: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listFacts\")(\n          (query: DescriptorFilterQuery) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.ListFacts({ query, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        listJurisdictions: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listJurisdictions\")(() =>\n          checkedRpcOperation(\n            RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n              Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                client.ListJurisdictions({ version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n              )\n            ),\n            protocol\n          )\n        ),\n        listRules: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listRules\")(\n          (query: DescriptorFilterQuery) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.ListRules({ query, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        listTaxYears: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listTaxYears\")(\n          (query: MetadataQuery) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.ListTaxYears({ query, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n      });\n    })\n  ).pipe(\n    Layer.provide(\n      Layer.effect(\n        RpcClient.Protocol,\n        HttpClient.HttpClient.pipe(\n          Effect.map((client) =>\n            client.pipe(\n              HttpClient.mapRequest(\n                HttpClientRequest.setUrl(new URL(\"/rpc\", origin).href)\n              ),\n              boundedCalculatorRpcHttpClient\n            )\n          ),\n          Effect.flatMap(RpcClient.makeProtocolHttp)\n        )\n      )\n    ),\n    Layer.provide(replySerialization)\n  );\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\";\n\nexport class AnalyticsConfigurationError extends Schema.TaggedError<AnalyticsConfigurationError>()(\n  \"AnalyticsConfigurationError\", { operation: Schema.Literal(\"configure\") }\n) {}\nexport class AnalyticsCaptureError extends Schema.TaggedError<AnalyticsCaptureError>()(\n  \"AnalyticsCaptureError\", {\n    operation: Schema.Literals([\"pageview\", \"calculator-use\", \"shutdown\"]),\n    reason: Schema.Literals([\"transport\", \"rejected\", \"deadline\", \"encoding\", \"identity\", \"response-size\", \"sdk\", \"closed\"]),\n  }\n) {}\nimport { Context } from \"effect\";\nimport type { Effect } from \"effect\";\nimport type { AnalyticsCaptureError } from \"./errors.js\";\nimport type { CalculatorUse, CaptureDisposition, CollectionPolicy, PageView } from \"./schemas.js\";\n\nexport class BackendAnalytics extends Context.Service<BackendAnalytics, {\n  readonly recordCalculatorUse: (input: CalculatorUse) => Effect.Effect<CaptureDisposition, AnalyticsCaptureError>;\n}>()(\"@taxkit/analytics/BackendAnalytics\") {}\nexport class BrowserAnalytics extends Context.Service<BrowserAnalytics, {\n  readonly recordPageView: (input: PageView) => Effect.Effect<CaptureDisposition, AnalyticsCaptureError>;\n  readonly getCollectionPolicy: Effect.Effect<CollectionPolicy, AnalyticsCaptureError>;\n}>()(\"@taxkit/analytics/BrowserAnalytics\") {}\n{\n  \"extends\": \"../../tsconfig.base.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2024\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"include\": [\n    \"src/**/*.ts\",\n    \"test/**/*.ts\",\n    \"vitest.config.ts\"\n  ]\n}\nimport { defaultServerConditions } from \"vite\";\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  resolve: { conditions: [\"source\", ...defaultServerConditions] },\n  test: { fileParallelism: false, include: [\"test/**/*.test.ts\"] },\n});\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7625},"formatted_output":"Manage retained TaxKit Production and one shared Preview PostHog project through\nAlchemy, following Common Practice's fixed US-region pattern, subject to the\nactual organisation/credentials in the reviewed provider plan. Local analytics\nis disabled. Ordinary Previews are disabled; an explicit controlled Preview\nproof can enable its Preview project. Production capture tokens are public\nwrite-only browser inputs; management/query credentials remain private in\nDoppler and never enter app output or bundles. No paid feature or billing\nchange is required by this scope.\n\nUse a private Effect browser service and React-owned Atom lifetime around the\nlatest `posthog-js`. Explicitly disable autocapture, recording, person profiles,\nsurveys and unnecessary automatic events; set Do Not Track handling explicitly.\nUse memory persistence with persistence disabled, rather than assuming local\nstorage cannot fall back to cookies. Qualify current shutdown/flush behaviour\nwithout promising network delivery on tab close. A synchronous closed allowlist\nafter SDK enrichment rejects unknown events/fields. Anonymous event identity\nand checked page metadata are the only browser context needed.\nKeep explicitly configured-off analytics distinct from invalid configuration:\ninvalid project/region/stage/token configuration has a named checked failure,\nnot a silent disabled result. After valid initialisation, capture/delivery is\nbest-effort and cannot fail a tax calculation or page. There is no old consent\nor identity migration to copy into the fresh application.\n\nThe Website may own a narrow same-origin POST event relay as the skill's\nanalytics exception to separate machine routes. Fix its regional upstream,\nchecked origin, path, query and media types. Bound whole-body read, forwarded\nbytes, upstream wait and reply size. Strip cookies, authorisation, IP-forwarding\nand tracing headers; do not follow or expose redirects. Preserve event UUIDs,\ntimestamps and upstream status; keep no-store. The SDK owns retries and the relay\nmakes one upstream attempt. Qualify the current SDK's actual `/e/` endpoint,\nbatch/compression/query behaviour; do not copy an older relay contract blindly.\n\n## Shared Axiom telemetry\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-008\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T004\",\n        \"CSF-T005\",\n        \"CSF-T006\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Manage retained TaxKit Production and shared Preview projects through a private Alchemy Resource/Provider and current Distilled PostHog, with checked organisation/region/ownership and safe management failures.\",\n        \"Implement explicit pageviews in a private React-owned browser service and one successful hosted-calculation event owner in the backend application; honour a checked browser opt-out without linking identities.\",\n        \"Use a synchronous final-enrichment allowlist, memory-only persistence, explicit DNT and disabled automatic/replay/person features. Local and ordinary Preview capture stay off; no consent dialog.\",\n        \"Implement the bounded same-origin event relay and native backend capture through owned Effect HTTP. Qualify actual current SDK transport/disposal and no duplicate events; retain best-effort delivery limits.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"apps/web analytics service/live adapter/consumer/relay and route event ownership\",\n        \"apps/api application successful-use capture and checked collection policy\",\n        \"packages/infrastructure PostHog provider/resources/bindings and qualified optional provider fixes\",\n        \"Analytics tests, app/infra READMEs, privacy/public copy and deployment/recovery runbook sections\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run test\",\n        \"bun run test:oxlint\",\nimport type {\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\n  DescriptorFilterQuery,\n  GetCalculatorGraphRequest,\n  GetCalculatorRequest,\n  MetadataQuery,\n} from \"@taxkit/calculators/schemas\";\nimport { Array, Effect, Layer, Schema } from \"effect\";\nimport type { Scope } from \"effect\";\nimport { FetchHttpClient, HttpClient, HttpClientRequest } from \"effect/http\";\nimport type { RpcClientError } from \"effect/rpc\";\nimport { Rpc, RpcClient, RpcSerialization } from \"effect/rpc\";\n\nimport {\n  boundedCalculatorRpcHttpClient,\n  calculatorRpcTransportFailure,\n} from \"./client-response.boundary.js\";\nimport type { CalculatorRpcExpectedError } from \"./errors.js\";\nimport {\n  CalculatorRpcDeadlineExceeded,\n  CalculatorRpcInvalidResponse,\n} from \"./errors.js\";\nimport { TaxKitRpcGroup } from \"./group.js\";\nimport { CalculatorRpcDeadline, CalculatorRpcVersion } from \"./schemas.js\";\nimport type { CalculatorRpcOrigin } from \"./schemas.js\";\nimport { TaxKitRpcClient } from \"./service.js\";\n\nclass RpcReplyDecodeDefect extends Schema.TaggedError<RpcReplyDecodeDefect>()(\n  \"RpcReplyDecodeDefect\",\n  {}\n) {}\n\n// Effect 4 caches the native exit Schema. Mark only its reply decoder's failure;\n// an independent adapter SchemaError remains a defect with its original identity.\nconst replySerialization = Layer.succeed(\n  RpcSerialization.RpcSerialization,\n  RpcSerialization.RpcSerialization.of({\n    ...RpcSerialization.json,\n    codecFor: <S extends Schema.Top>(schema: S) => {\n      const codec = RpcSerialization.json.codecFor(schema);\n      return Array.some(\n        Array.fromIterable(TaxKitRpcGroup.requests.values()),\n        (procedure) => schema.ast === Rpc.exitSchema(procedure).ast\n      )\n        ? codec.pipe(\n            Schema.catchDecoding<typeof codec>(() =>\n              Effect.die(new RpcReplyDecodeDefect())\n            )\n          )\n        : codec;\n    },\n  })\n);\n\n// The concrete native operation owns its client scope, complete-response budget\n// and safe failure projection. This accepts an Effect, never a raw-client callback.\nconst checkedRpcOperation = <A>(\n  operation: Effect.Effect<\n    A,\n    typeof CalculatorRpcExpectedError.Type | RpcClientError.RpcClientError,\n    Scope.Scope | RpcClient.Protocol\n  >,\n  protocol: RpcClient.Protocol[\"Service\"]\n) =>\n  operation.pipe(\n    Effect.scoped,\n    Effect.provideService(RpcClient.Protocol, protocol),\n    Effect.provideService(HttpClient.TracerDisabledWhen, () => true),\n    Effect.provideService(FetchHttpClient.RequestInit, {\n      credentials: \"omit\",\n      redirect: \"error\",\n    }),\n    Effect.timeoutOrElse({\n      duration: CalculatorRpcDeadline,\n      orElse: () => Effect.fail(new CalculatorRpcDeadlineExceeded()),\n    }),\n    Effect.catchTag(\"RpcClientError\", (error) =>\n      Effect.fail(calculatorRpcTransportFailure(error))\n    ),\n    Effect.catchDefect((defect) =>\n      Schema.is(RpcReplyDecodeDefect)(defect)\n        ? Effect.fail(new CalculatorRpcInvalidResponse())\n        : Effect.die(defect)\n    )\n  );\n\n// The app supplies its matching-stage HttpClient. The Layer retains transport\n// configuration, while each named operation owns its native client scope. A\n// Worker can suspend between requests: retaining a receive-loop fibre acquired\n// by an earlier request leaves later calls waiting. No runtime or Layer is built\n// by a calculation; native RPC creation and finalisation run in its own scope.\nexport const TaxKitRpcClientLive = (origin: CalculatorRpcOrigin) =>\n  Layer.effect(\n    TaxKitRpcClient,\n    Effect.gen(function* () {\n      const protocol = yield* RpcClient.Protocol;\n      return TaxKitRpcClient.of({\n        calculate: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.calculate\")(\n          (request: CalculatorRunServiceRequest) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.Calculate({ request, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        getCalculator: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.getCalculator\")(\n          (request: GetCalculatorRequest) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.GetCalculator({\n                    request,\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\n                  })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        getCalculatorGraph: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.getCalculatorGraph\")(\n          (request: GetCalculatorGraphRequest) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.GetCalculatorGraph({\n                    request,\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\n                  })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        getCalculatorSchema: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.getCalculatorSchema\")(\n          (request: GetCalculatorRequest) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.GetCalculatorSchema({\n                    request,\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\n                  })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        listCalculators: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listCalculators\")(\n          (query: MetadataQuery) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.ListCalculators({\n                    query,\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\n                  })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        listFacts: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listFacts\")(\n          (query: DescriptorFilterQuery) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.ListFacts({ query, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        listJurisdictions: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listJurisdictions\")(() =>\n          checkedRpcOperation(\n            RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n              Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                client.ListJurisdictions({ version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n              )\n            ),\n            protocol\n          )\n        ),\n        listRules: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listRules\")(\n          (query: DescriptorFilterQuery) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.ListRules({ query, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n        listTaxYears: Effect.fn(\"TaxKitRpcClient.listTaxYears\")(\n          (query: MetadataQuery) =>\n            checkedRpcOperation(\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\n                  client.ListTaxYears({ query, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\n                )\n              ),\n              protocol\n            )\n        ),\n      });\n    })\n  ).pipe(\n    Layer.provide(\n      Layer.effect(\n        RpcClient.Protocol,\n        HttpClient.HttpClient.pipe(\n          Effect.map((client) =>\n            client.pipe(\n              HttpClient.mapRequest(\n                HttpClientRequest.setUrl(new URL(\"/rpc\", origin).href)\n              ),\n              boundedCalculatorRpcHttpClient\n            )\n          ),\n          Effect.flatMap(RpcClient.makeProtocolHttp)\n        )\n      )\n    ),\n    Layer.provide(replySerialization)\n  );\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\";\n\nexport class AnalyticsConfigurationError extends Schema.TaggedError<AnalyticsConfigurationError>()(\n  \"AnalyticsConfigurationError\", { operation: Schema.Literal(\"configure\") }\n) {}\nexport class AnalyticsCaptureError extends Schema.TaggedError<AnalyticsCaptureError>()(\n  \"AnalyticsCaptureError\", {\n    operation: Schema.Literals([\"pageview\", \"calculator-use\", \"shutdown\"]),\n    reason: Schema.Literals([\"transport\", \"rejected\", \"deadline\", \"encoding\", \"identity\", \"response-size\", \"sdk\", \"closed\"]),\n  }\n) {}\nimport { Context } from \"effect\";\nimport type { Effect } from \"effect\";\nimport type { AnalyticsCaptureError } from \"./errors.js\";\nimport type { CalculatorUse, CaptureDisposition, CollectionPolicy, PageView } from \"./schemas.js\";\n\nexport class BackendAnalytics extends Context.Service<BackendAnalytics, {\n  readonly recordCalculatorUse: (input: CalculatorUse) => Effect.Effect<CaptureDisposition, AnalyticsCaptureError>;\n}>()(\"@taxkit/analytics/BackendAnalytics\") {}\nexport class BrowserAnalytics extends Context.Service<BrowserAnalytics, {\n  readonly recordPageView: (input: PageView) => Effect.Effect<CaptureDisposition, AnalyticsCaptureError>;\n  readonly getCollectionPolicy: Effect.Effect<CollectionPolicy, AnalyticsCaptureError>;\n}>()(\"@taxkit/analytics/BrowserAnalytics\") {}\n{\n  \"extends\": \"../../tsconfig.base.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2024\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"include\": [\n    \"src/**/*.ts\",\n    \"test/**/*.ts\",\n    \"vitest.config.ts\"\n  ]\n}\nimport { defaultServerConditions } from \"vite\";\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  resolve: { conditions: [\"source\", ...defaultServerConditions] },\n  test: { fileParallelism: false, include: [\"test/**/*.test.ts\"] },\n});\n"},"started_at_ms":1791368352089,"completed_at_ms":1791368352089}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:19:12.139Z","ordinal":68173,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a115df-d18b-7691-b61f-d4e8af77a16e","call_id":"call_ee41d13ea69041d88e498976a8d9f99a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"8d5440\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007625,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3694,\"output\":\"Manage retained TaxKit Production and one shared Preview PostHog project through\\nAlchemy, following Common Practice's fixed US-region pattern, subject to the\\nactual organisation/credentials in the reviewed provider plan. Local analytics\\nis disabled. Ordinary Previews are disabled; an explicit controlled Preview\\nproof can enable its Preview project. Production capture tokens are public\\nwrite-only browser inputs; management/query credentials remain private in\\nDoppler and never enter app output or bundles. No paid feature or billing\\nchange is required by this scope.\\n\\nUse a private Effect browser service and React-owned Atom lifetime around the\\nlatest `posthog-js`. Explicitly disable autocapture, recording, person profiles,\\nsurveys and unnecessary automatic events; set Do Not Track handling explicitly.\\nUse memory persistence with persistence disabled, rather than assuming local\\nstorage cannot fall back to cookies. Qualify current shutdown/flush behaviour\\nwithout promising network delivery on tab close. A synchronous closed allowlist\\nafter SDK enrichment rejects unknown events/fields. Anonymous event identity\\nand checked page metadata are the only browser context needed.\\nKeep explicitly configured-off analytics distinct from invalid configuration:\\ninvalid project/region/stage/token configuration has a named checked failure,\\nnot a silent disabled result. After valid initialisation, capture/delivery is\\nbest-effort and cannot fail a tax calculation or page. There is no old consent\\nor identity migration to copy into the fresh application.\\n\\nThe Website may own a narrow same-origin POST event relay as the skill's\\nanalytics exception to separate machine routes. Fix its regional upstream,\\nchecked origin, path, query and media types. Bound whole-body read, forwarded\\nbytes, upstream wait and reply size. Strip cookies, authorisation, IP-forwarding\\nand tracing headers; do not follow or expose redirects. Preserve event UUIDs,\\ntimestamps and upstream status; keep no-store. The SDK owns retries and the relay\\nmakes one upstream attempt. Qualify the current SDK's actual `/e/` endpoint,\\nbatch/compression/query behaviour; do not copy an older relay contract blindly.\\n\\n## Shared Axiom telemetry\\n      \\\"acceptedFindingIds\\\": [],\\n      \\\"requirementIds\\\": [\\n        \\\"CSF-008\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"dependsOn\\\": [\\n        \\\"CSF-T004\\\",\\n        \\\"CSF-T005\\\",\\n        \\\"CSF-T006\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"goal\\\": \\\"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": [\\n        \\\"Manage retained TaxKit Production and shared Preview projects through a private Alchemy Resource/Provider and current Distilled PostHog, with checked organisation/region/ownership and safe management failures.\\\",\\n        \\\"Implement explicit pageviews in a private React-owned browser service and one successful hosted-calculation event owner in the backend application; honour a checked browser opt-out without linking identities.\\\",\\n        \\\"Use a synchronous final-enrichment allowlist, memory-only persistence, explicit DNT and disabled automatic/replay/person features. Local and ordinary Preview capture stay off; no consent dialog.\\\",\\n        \\\"Implement the bounded same-origin event relay and native backend capture through owned Effect HTTP. Qualify actual current SDK transport/disposal and no duplicate events; retain best-effort delivery limits.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"outputs\\\": [\\n        \\\"apps/web analytics service/live adapter/consumer/relay and route event ownership\\\",\\n        \\\"apps/api application successful-use capture and checked collection policy\\\",\\n        \\\"packages/infrastructure PostHog provider/resources/bindings and qualified optional provider fixes\\\",\\n        \\\"Analytics tests, app/infra READMEs, privacy/public copy and deployment/recovery runbook sections\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"implementationPrompt\\\": \\\"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\\\",\\n      \\\"mandatoryVerification\\\": [\\n        \\\"bun run test\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run test:oxlint\\\",\\nimport type {\\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\\n  DescriptorFilterQuery,\\n  GetCalculatorGraphRequest,\\n  GetCalculatorRequest,\\n  MetadataQuery,\\n} from \\\"@taxkit/calculators/schemas\\\";\\nimport { Array, Effect, Layer, Schema } from \\\"effect\\\";\\nimport type { Scope } from \\\"effect\\\";\\nimport { FetchHttpClient, HttpClient, HttpClientRequest } from \\\"effect/http\\\";\\nimport type { RpcClientError } from \\\"effect/rpc\\\";\\nimport { Rpc, RpcClient, RpcSerialization } from \\\"effect/rpc\\\";\\n\\nimport {\\n  boundedCalculatorRpcHttpClient,\\n  calculatorRpcTransportFailure,\\n} from \\\"./client-response.boundary.js\\\";\\nimport type { CalculatorRpcExpectedError } from \\\"./errors.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  CalculatorRpcDeadlineExceeded,\\n  CalculatorRpcInvalidResponse,\\n} from \\\"./errors.js\\\";\\nimport { TaxKitRpcGroup } from \\\"./group.js\\\";\\nimport { CalculatorRpcDeadline, CalculatorRpcVersion } from \\\"./schemas.js\\\";\\nimport type { CalculatorRpcOrigin } from \\\"./schemas.js\\\";\\nimport { TaxKitRpcClient } from \\\"./service.js\\\";\\n\\nclass RpcReplyDecodeDefect extends Schema.TaggedError<RpcReplyDecodeDefect>()(\\n  \\\"RpcReplyDecodeDefect\\\",\\n  {}\\n) {}\\n\\n// Effect 4 caches the native exit Schema. Mark only its reply decoder's failure;\\n// an independent adapter SchemaError remains a defect with its original identity.\\nconst replySerialization = Layer.succeed(\\n  RpcSerialization.RpcSerialization,\\n  RpcSerialization.RpcSerialization.of({\\n    ...RpcSerialization.json,\\n    codecFor: <S extends Schema.Top>(schema: S) => {\\n      const codec = RpcSerialization.json.codecFor(schema);\\n      return Array.some(\\n        Array.fromIterable(TaxKitRpcGroup.requests.values()),\\n        (procedure) => schema.ast === Rpc.exitSchema(procedure).ast\\n      )\\n        ? codec.pipe(\\n            Schema.catchDecoding<typeof codec>(() =>\\n              Effect.die(new RpcReplyDecodeDefect())\\n            )\\n          )\\n        : codec;\\n    },\\n  })\\n);\\n\\n// The concrete native operation owns its client scope, complete-response budget\\n// and safe failure projection. This accepts an Effect, never a raw-client callback.\\nconst checkedRpcOperation = <A>(\\n  operation: Effect.Effect<\\n    A,\\n    typeof CalculatorRpcExpectedError.Type | RpcClientError.RpcClientError,\\n    Scope.Scope | RpcClient.Protocol\\n  >,\\n  protocol: RpcClient.Protocol[\\\"Service\\\"]\\n) =>\\n  operation.pipe(\\n    Effect.scoped,\\n    Effect.provideService(RpcClient.Protocol, protocol),\\n    Effect.provideService(HttpClient.TracerDisabledWhen, () => true),\\n    Effect.provideService(FetchHttpClient.RequestInit, {\\n      credentials: \\\"omit\\\",\\n      redirect: \\\"error\\\",\\n    }),\\n    Effect.timeoutOrElse({\\n      duration: CalculatorRpcDeadline,\\n      orElse: () => Effect.fail(new CalculatorRpcDeadlineExceeded()),\\n    }),\\n    Effect.catchTag(\\\"RpcClientError\\\", (error) =>\\n      Effect.fail(calculatorRpcTransportFailure(error))\\n    ),\\n    Effect.catchDefect((defect) =>\\n      Schema.is(RpcReplyDecodeDefect)(defect)\\n        ? Effect.fail(new CalculatorRpcInvalidResponse())\\n        : Effect.die(defect)\\n    )\\n  );\\n\\n// The app supplies its matching-stage HttpClient. The Layer retains transport\\n// configuration, while each named operation owns its native client scope. A\\n// Worker can suspend between requests: retaining a receive-loop fibre acquired\\n// by an earlier request leaves later calls waiting. No runtime or Layer is built\\n// by a calculation; native RPC creation and finalisation run in its own scope.\\nexport const TaxKitRpcClientLive = (origin: CalculatorRpcOrigin) =>\\n  Layer.effect(\\n    TaxKitRpcClient,\\n    Effect.gen(function* () {\\n      const protocol = yield* RpcClient.Protocol;\\n      return TaxKitRpcClient.of({\\n        calculate: Effect.fn(\\\"TaxKitRpcClient.calculate\\\")(\\n          (request: CalculatorRunServiceRequest) =>\\n            checkedRpcOperation(\\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\\n                  client.Calculate({ request, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\\n                )\\n              ),\\n              protocol\\n            )\\n        ),\\n        getCalculator: Effect.fn(\\\"TaxKitRpcClient.getCalculator\\\")(\\n          (request: GetCalculatorRequest) =>\\n            checkedRpcOperation(\\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\\n                  client.GetCalculator({\\n                    request,\\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\\n                  })\\n                )\\n              ),\\n              protocol\\n            )\\n        ),\\n        getCalculatorGraph: Effect.fn(\\\"TaxKitRpcClient.getCalculatorGraph\\\")(\\n          (request: GetCalculatorGraphRequest) =>\\n            checkedRpcOperation(\\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\\n                  client.GetCalculatorGraph({\\n                    request,\\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\\n                  })\\n                )\\n              ),\\n              protocol\\n            )\\n        ),\\n        getCalculatorSchema: Effect.fn(\\\"TaxKitRpcClient.getCalculatorSchema\\\")(\\n          (request: GetCalculatorRequest) =>\\n            checkedRpcOperation(\\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\\n                  client.GetCalculatorSchema({\\n                    request,\\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\\n                  })\\n                )\\n              ),\\n              protocol\\n            )\\n        ),\\n        listCalculators: Effect.fn(\\\"TaxKitRpcClient.listCalculators\\\")(\\n          (query: MetadataQuery) =>\\n            checkedRpcOperation(\\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\\n                  client.ListCalculators({\\n                    query,\\n                    version: CalculatorRpcVersion,\\n                  })\\n                )\\n              ),\\n              protocol\\n            )\\n        ),\\n        listFacts: Effect.fn(\\\"TaxKitRpcClient.listFacts\\\")(\\n          (query: DescriptorFilterQuery) =>\\n            checkedRpcOperation(\\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\\n                  client.ListFacts({ query, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\\n                )\\n              ),\\n              protocol\\n            )\\n        ),\\n        listJurisdictions: Effect.fn(\\\"TaxKitRpcClient.listJurisdictions\\\")(() =>\\n          checkedRpcOperation(\\n            RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\\n              Effect.flatMap((client) =>\\n                client.ListJurisdictions({ version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\\n              )\\n            ),\\n            protocol\\n          )\\n        ),\\n        listRules: Effect.fn(\\\"TaxKitRpcClient.listRules\\\")(\\n          (query: DescriptorFilterQuery) =>\\n            checkedRpcOperation(\\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\\n                  client.ListRules({ query, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\\n                )\\n              ),\\n              protocol\\n            )\\n        ),\\n        listTaxYears: Effect.fn(\\\"TaxKitRpcClient.listTaxYears\\\")(\\n          (query: MetadataQuery) =>\\n            checkedRpcOperation(\\n              RpcClient.make(TaxKitRpcGroup, { disableTracing: true }).pipe(\\n                Effect.flatMap((client) =>\\n                  client.ListTaxYears({ query, version: CalculatorRpcVersion })\\n                )\\n              ),\\n              protocol\\n            )\\n        ),\\n      });\\n    })\\n  ).pipe(\\n    Layer.provide(\\n      Layer.effect(\\n        RpcClient.Protocol,\\n        HttpClient.HttpClient.pipe(\\n          Effect.map((client) =>\\n            client.pipe(\\n              HttpClient.mapRequest(\\n                HttpClientRequest.setUrl(new URL(\\\"/rpc\\\", origin).href)\\n              ),\\n              boundedCalculatorRpcHttpClient\\n            )\\n          ),\\n          Effect.flatMap(RpcClient.makeProtocolHttp)\\n        )\\n      )\\n    ),\\n    Layer.provide(replySerialization)\\n  );\\nimport { Schema } from \\\"effect\\\";\\n\\nexport class AnalyticsConfigurationError extends Schema.TaggedError<AnalyticsConfigurationError>()(\\n  \\\"AnalyticsConfigurationError\\\", { operation: Schema.Literal(\\\"configure\\\") }\\n) {}\\nexport class AnalyticsCaptureError extends Schema.TaggedError<AnalyticsCaptureError>()(\\n  \\\"AnalyticsCaptureError\\\", {\\n    operation: Schema.Literals([\\\"pageview\\\", \\\"calculator-use\\\", \\\"shutdown\\\"]),\\n    reason: Schema.Literals([\\\"transport\\\", \\\"rejected\\\", \\\"deadline\\\", \\\"encoding\\\", \\\"identity\\\", \\\"response-size\\\", \\\"sdk\\\", \\\"closed\\\"]),\\n  }\\n) {}\\nimport { Context } from \\\"effect\\\";\\nimport type { Effect } from \\\"effect\\\";\\nimport type { AnalyticsCaptureError } from \\\"./errors.js\\\";\\nimport type { CalculatorUse, CaptureDisposition, CollectionPolicy, PageView } from \\\"./schemas.js\\\";\\n\\nexport class BackendAnalytics extends Context.Service<BackendAnalytics, {\\n  readonly recordCalculatorUse: (input: CalculatorUse) => Effect.Effect<CaptureDisposition, AnalyticsCaptureError>;\\n}>()(\\\"@taxkit/analytics/BackendAnalytics\\\") {}\\nexport class BrowserAnalytics extends Context.Service<BrowserAnalytics, {\\n  readonly recordPageView: (input: PageView) => Effect.Effect<CaptureDisposition, AnalyticsCaptureError>;\\n  readonly getCollectionPolicy: Effect.Effect<CollectionPolicy, AnalyticsCaptureError>;\\n}>()(\\\"@taxkit/analytics/BrowserAnalytics\\\") {}\\n{\\n  \\\"extends\\\": \\\"../../tsconfig.base.json\\\",\\n  \\\"compilerOptions\\\": {\\n    \\\"lib\\\": [\\n      \\\"ES2024\\\",\\n      \\\"DOM\\\",\\n      \\\"DOM.Iterable\\\"\\n    ]\\